-- DLC Dragonforge - Dragon's Dogma 2 (REFramework script)
-- Dragonforging like in the first game, for the Dark Arisen DLC spoils: when you or your pawns slay a dragon-type
-- enemy, one random equipped DLC spoil of yours (appraised or Smithed weapon, shield, helmet, body or leg armour)
-- gains a dragonforge level, up to 3. Each level adds a third of the bonus the official DLC tables give the
-- dragonforge level (scaled to the item); the 3rd also halves the item's weight. The dragonforge mark on the item's
-- card changes colour with the level.
-- Those items have no upgrade tables in the game, so this script adds tables for them. The game only allows the
-- dragonforge level on top of three smith steps; the smith type stored in those (hidden) steps is the level counter:
-- Vernworth = level 1, Battahl = level 2, Elf = level 3 (the "Dragon" type of 1.0/1.1 forges = level 3 too).
-- The dragonforge is NOT written to your save file: the list is kept per save slot in
-- reframework/data/DLCDragonforge.json, taken off the items while the game writes a save and put back right after.
-- Without the mod your items are plain DLC items again. Uninstall with the game closed.
-- Menu: REFramework (Insert) > Script Generated UI > DLC Dragonforge
local VERSION = "1.3"
local DATA = "DLCDragonforge.json"
local ENH_DRAGON, ENH_UNLIMIT = 3, 4

-- [item id] = { "w"/"a", name, dragonforge entry (1/3), { 3 level-2 steps }, { 3 level-3 steps } } - generated from
-- the game's own DLC upgrade tables (src/build_levels.py)
